# core.autocrlf is `input` here, which asks git to rewrite line endings in anything it
# decides is text. It decides by looking for a NUL in the first 8000 bytes, and the sprite
# sheets and the synthesised impact both happen to carry one early enough to be classified
# correctly today. Saying so outright is two lines, and the failure it forecloses is a
# silently corrupted asset on a checkout that never ran the guess the same way.
*.png binary
*.wav binary
*.glb binary
*.ktx2 binary

# The generated scenes are JSON with one long base64 buffer per file. Diffing them is
# noise -- what changed is never legible at the character level -- and merging them is
# never right, because the accessor offsets either side of a conflict have already moved.
*.gltf -diff -merge
